      "knowledge_point": "Simplifying an Expression Using the Alternate Forms of the Cotangent-Cosecant Identity",
      "problem": "Simplify $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we multiply the numerator and the denominator of our expression by $\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta -1}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta \\,(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1)}{{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the identity ${csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1={cot}^{2}⁡\\theta $, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta \\,(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1)}{{csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta \\,(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1)}{{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\cancel{\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }\\,(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1)}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\,(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1) \\\\  & =\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}\\,(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,(\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
